<title>INDIA: India HDFC 96/97 1st half net up 43 pct.</title>
<headline>India HDFC 96/97 1st half net up 43 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit		   1,087.85 vs   762.46</p>
<p>    Income from operations   5,793.95 vs 4,404.93</p>
<p>    Other income		     8.27 vs    60.39</p>
<p>    Interest costs	     3,946.57 vs 3,155.50</p>
<p>    Other expenses		 297.80 vs   213.16</p>
<p>    Profit before tax	  1,367.85 vs   990.66</p>
<p>    Provision for tax	    280.00 vs   228.20</p>
<p>Note: Housing Development Finance Corporation Ltd (HDFC) said loan disbursements in the first half were up 25 percent at 9.05 billion rupees. It said its deposit base rose to 31.25 billion rupees in September from 25.13 billion in March 1996. The results are unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
